            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed all 7 changed paths in full. The atomicfile change adds a typed dirFlushError that keeps the old message and wraps the underlying error. Its Is method matches only ErrDirNotFlushed, so it introduces no data exposure and does not widen any path handling.",
              "publishError in engine/review/fsstore/bypath.go checks fs.ErrExist before ErrDirNotFlushed. A failed directory flush therefore cannot be mistaken for a taken name, and a published result is reported as stored (app.ErrNotFlushed) rather than retried and duplicated. The symlink and ErrChanged protections on the by-path store are unchanged.",
              "The recordFailed refactor in engine/cmd/review.go keeps the exit codes: 2 for a refused reply and 1 for anything else, including a handoff write failure. The change to the handoff-failure path is small, and I found no input that now exits with the wrong code.",
              "The change to held_linux.go touches only a comment. The CHANGELOG and the tests add no runtime behavior.",
              "I found no secrets, no unsafe input handling and no dependency changes in this candidate."
            ]
          }
        }
