            "evidence": [
              "engine/atomicfile/atomicfile.go: dirFlushError keeps the original message text and Unwrap returns the underlying flush error. Is matches ErrDirNotFlushed. Callers that matched the old wrapped error still work, and the new sentinel only adds information.",
              "engine/review/fsstore/bypath.go: publishError maps a failed directory flush after the link to app.ErrNotFlushed. The fallback platform no longer reports a stored result as a failure, so a retry cannot store a duplicate. The taken-name check runs first, so ErrExist and ErrNotFlushed stay distinct. The test covers both cases plus the generic fallback.",
              "engine/cmd/review.go: recordFailed is a pure extraction of the earlier closure. A handoff write failure still exits 1, because that error does not wrap a refusal. The stderr text is unchanged.",
